      .page.about.us(data-url="/about/us")
        .col1
          h2.etflabs_logo &nbsp;
        .col2
          p ETF Labs and Foreside have combined a unique set of capabilities and licenses to create the world's first benchmark index: the ETF 50, symbol ETFF. Additionally, 3 products a year for the first 3 years are to be launched by the firm.
          p The U.S. ETF industry is controlled by the top three providers who currently control 83.2% of the US market.  As of March 31, 2013, BlackRock’s iShares family controlled $598 billion, or 40.8% of the U.S. ETF industry . State Street had $345 billion of ETF assets, or 23.5% market share followed by Vanguard’s ETF assets totaling $277 billion for an 18.9% market share. Barriers to entry include: cost, SEC exemptive relief process, acquisition process and technical know-how. This business opportunity may represent the easiest point of entry into the rapidly growing ETF industry.
      .page.about.contact(data-url="/about/contact")
        .col1
          h2.etflabs_logo &nbsp;
        .col2
          h3 Lee Morin
          h4 Director, Web and Database Develepment
          p 3 Canal Plaza Suite 100
          p Portland, ME 04101
          a(href="mailto:lmorin@foreside.com") lmorin@foreside.com
      .page.partner.foreside(data-url="/partners/foreside")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://foreside.com/", target="_blank") Foreside 
          h3 Sponsor/Advisor
          a.site_link(href="http://foreside.com/", target="_blank") www.foreside.com
        .col2 Foreside serves separate account managers and the sponsors of open-end, closed-end, exchange traded and alternative investment funds, including commodity pools, with Sarbanes-Oxley, independent CCO, CCO support, registered representative, and active and statutory distribution services.  Today, Foreside employs more than 80 experienced professionals including securities attorneys, certified public accountants and key fund officers.  Foreside acts as distributor for over 70 registrants with AUM of over $500 billion, and maintains over 6,000 dealer agreements and over 140 exchange-traded product AP Agreements.  Foreside has provided services to Investment Advisers, Broker-Dealers, CPOs/CTAs, Mutual Funds, Hedge Funds, Private Equity Funds, and Investment Bankers.
      .page.partner.ise(data-url="/partners/ise")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.ise.com/", target="_blank") International Securities Exchange 
          h3 Index Provider
          a.site_link(href="http://www.ise.com/", target="_blank") www.ise.com
        .col2 The International Securities Exchange (ISE) launched in May, 2000 as the first all-electronic options exchange in the US. The ISE is a regulated securities exchange with over 150 member firms, more than 30 of which are major US broker-dealers and market makers including Goldman Sachs, Citigroup, Citadel, Merrill Lynch, Morgan Stanley, JP Morgan, UBS and Credit Suisse.  The ISE ETF Ventures group develops indexes that are the basis for new exchange-trade products (ETPs), and provides financial, marketing, and other support for new ETPs.  ISE was acquired by Deutsche Borse AG (DBAG) in 2007.
      .page.partner.statestreet(data-url="/partners/statestreet")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.statestreet.com/", target="_blank") State Street
          h3 &nbsp;
          a.site_link(href="http://statestreet.com/", target="_blank") www.statestreet.com
        .col2
          p State Street is one of the world's leading providers of financial services to institutional investors including investment servicing, investment management and investment research and trading.  With US $23.4-trillion in assets under custody and administration, and US $2.1trillion* under management as of September 30, 2012 State Street operates in 29 countries and more than 100 geographic markets.  State Street pioneered ETF servicing as the service provider for the first ETF product launched in the US in 1993. State Street has consistently been positioned at the top of industry rankings.  It was named Best Online Bank among FX trading systems (Currenex), No. 1 US institutional tax-exempt assets, No. 1 servicer of alternative assets globally, No. 1 servicer of retail assets globally, No. 1 servicer of equity assets globally, No. 1 servicer of hedge fund assets globally, as well as being named The Most Recognized ETF Brand.
          p *This AUM includes assets of SPDR Gold Trust (approximately $75.3 billion as of September 30, 2012) for which State Street Global Markets, LLC an affiliate of State Street Global Advisors serves as the marketing agent.
      .page.partner.klgates(data-url="/partners/klgates")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://www.klgates.com/", target="_blank") K&L Gates 
          h3 K&L Gates's Role 
          a.site_link(href="http://klgates.com/", target="_blank") www.klgates.com
        .col2
          p K&L Gates is one of the premier Investment Management practices in the United States.  K&L Gates is comprised of more than 2,000 lawyers who practice in 46 different office located on five continents: Anchorage, Austin, Beijing, Berlin, Boston, Brisbane, Brussels, Charleston, Charlotte, Chicago, Dallas, Doha, Dubai, Fort Worth, Frankfurt, Harrisburg, Hong Kong, London, Los Angeles, Melbourne, Miami, Milan, Moscow, Newark, New York, Orange County, Palo Alto, Paris, Perth, Pittsburgh, Portland, Raleigh, Research Triangle Park, San Diego, San Francisco, Sao Paulo, Seattle, Seoul, Shanghai, Singapore, Spokane, Sydney, Taipei, Tokyo, Warsaw, and Washington.
          p K&L Gates represents leading global corporations, growth and middle market companies, capital markets participants and entrepreneurs in every major industry group as well as public sector entities, educational institutions, philanthropic organizations and individuals.  Our practice is a robust full market practice – cutting edge, complex and dynamic, at once regional, national and international in scope.  Over each of the last four years our revenues exceeded $1 Billion and, as stated in the July 2010 issue of the UK Publication Legal Business, the firm "has further cemented its position as the Global 100s fastest growing firm."
      .page.partner.two-n(data-url="/partners/two-n")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://two-n.com/", target="_blank") Two-N, Inc. 
          h3 ETF Mapper
          a.site_link(href="http://two-n.com/", target="_blank") www.two-n.com
        .col2 Two-N, Inc. is a New York Based design studio specializing in design and development of data visualizations. We work with our clients and their diverse – and often complex – datasets to produce interactive applications, data displays, user interface designs, and infographics. Our design philosophy promotes experimentation, innovation and process adaptability throughout the lifecycle of any project. Two-N has been engaged in a number of exciting data visualization projects, ranging from financial trading data to economic data, demographic data, and other complex data sets across a number of leading organizations, including Bloomberg LP, The New York Stock Exchange, SAP, WNYC, and Google Labs.
      .page.partner.cnbc(data-url="/partners/cnbc")
        .col1
          h2.partner_logo
            a(href="http://cnbc.com/", target="_blank") CNBC
          h3 Media Partner
          a.site_link(href="http://two-n.com/", target="_blank") www.cnbc.com
        .col2 Seitan ex McSweeney's labore mumblecore direct trade. Mixtape hoodie veniam, McSweeney's cray ad bicycle rights wolf do put a bird on it voluptate messenger bag. Readymade blog fingerstache Truffaut, next level irure hashtag craft beer small batch minim. Asymmetrical gluten-free vero +1. Put a bird on it banh mi retro, authentic Shoreditch whatever quis dreamcatcher ethnic. DIY aute Thundercats chillwave iPhone. Dolore post-ironic +1, trust fund anim twee esse sint consectetur beard selvage raw denim commodo.
      
      .page.product.composite(data-url="/products/etfcomposite")
        .col1
          img.product_logo(src="/images/domains/foreside/etf_composite_quote_logo.png")
          a.product_link(href="#") View on Bloomberg:&nbsp;
            strong ETFCOMP
          a.product_link(href="#") View on Yahoo Finance:&nbsp;
            strong ^ETFCOMP
          a.document_link
            img(src="/images/domains/foreside/methodology.png")
            .product_link(href="#") Download Composite Methodology
        .col2
          p The FORESIDE ETF Composite™ Index has been created to provide investors with a product allowing them to track US ETFs. The Index uses an equal weighted allocation across the constituents. Index components are reviewed semi-annually for eligibility, and the weights are re-set according to that distribution. 
          h3 Component Eligibility Requirements
          p All of the following requirements must be met in order for a security to be eligible for inclusion:
          ol
            li The component security must be an Exchange Traded Fund listed in the US.
            li The component security must not be an Exchange Traded Note.
            li The component security must not be levered or inverse.
            li The component security must have over $5 million in assets.

      .page.product.etf50(data-url="/products/etf50")
        .col1
          img.product_logo(src="/images/domains/foreside/etf_50_quote_logo.png")
          a.product_link(href="#") View on Bloomberg:&nbsp;
            strong ETFF
          a.product_link(href="#") View on Yahoo Finance:&nbsp;
            strong ^ETFF
          a.document_link
            img(src="/images/domains/foreside/methodology.png")
            .product_link(href="#") Download Composite Methodology
        .col2
          p The ISE ETF 50™ Index has been created to provide investors with a product allowing them to track US ETFs.  The ISE ETF 50™ Index quantitatively ranks ETFs by fees, volatility and performance and selects the top 25 equity-focused funds and the top 25 non-equity focused funds. The Index uses an equal weighted allocation across the constituents. Index components are reviewed quarterly for eligibility, and the weights are re-set according to that distribution.
          h3 Component Eligibility Requirements
          p All of the following requirements must be met in order for a security to be eligible for inclusion:
          ol
            li US Exchange listed ETFs
              span.comment Includes 40 Act and 33 Act products 
            li No levered products – no products tracking multiple of index daily returns
              span.comment Avoids path dependent index tracking problems
            li No ETNs
              span.comment Avoids issuer credit risk
            li ETF assets > $100 Million
            li ETF daily value traded > $1 Million
              span.comment Only large and liquid ETFs
            li Weight distribution limits
            li Top 50 after ranking equally by three criteria:
            li Fees 
            li Volatility over the last quarter
            li Total return performance over the last quarter
            li Equal-weighted portfolio
              span.comment Reduces concentration in any particular ETF
            li Rebalanced quarterly
            li Reconstituted quarterly
              span.comment All selection criteria applied each quarter
            li No fund tracking this ISE index methodology may be included in the Top 50
      .page.product.etf25(data-url="/products/etf25")
        .col1
          img.product_logo(src="/images/domains/foreside/etf_25_quote_logo.png")
        .col2
          p The index tracks a portfolio of 25 exchange-traded funds (ETFs), that are listed on a regulated securities exchange in the US and are equity-focused.  The constituent ETFs must meet a variety of eligibility requirements that focus on, among other things, assets under management, liquidity, and share price performance.  The index excludes exchange-traded notes and leveraged exchange-traded products (ETPs).
      .page.product.etf25(data-url="/products/etf25ne")
        .col1
          img.product_logo(src="/images/domains/foreside/etf_25_quote_logo.png")
        .col2
          p The index tracks a portfolio of 25 exchange-traded funds (ETFs), grantor trusts, exchange-traded commodity pools, and other such similar products, that are listed on a regulated securities exchange in the US and are non-equity focused.  The constituent ETFs must meet a variety of eligibility requirements that focus on, among other things, assets under management, liquidity, and share price performance.  The index excludes exchange-traded notes and leveraged exchange-traded products (ETPs).
      .page.product.etf25(data-url="/products/etfmapper")
        .col1
          img.product_logo(src="/images/domains/nyse/stockmapper_logo.png")
          a.document_link
            img(src="/images/domains/foreside/methodology.png")
            .product_link(href="#") StockMapper White Paper
        .col2
          p Stockmapper was created to provide a snapshot of the market along with detailed quotes, news feeds and historical graphs. Stockmapper was designed and developed by Two-N, Inc. a New York based data visualization agency. It can be configured and restyled to display any collection of financial instruments so that agents may use it for special agent processes, financial planners may use it to manage client portfolios, retailers may use is to build portfolio's and institutions may use it for an viewing specific account information.
